    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is headlined by a formidable top tier, led by **Kyle Tucker** (79.56) and **Andy Pages** (69.91). Both outfielders draw a high-upside matchup against Trevor Rogers, where positive wind conditions and favorable park factors have elevated their efficiency scores significantly beyond their base projections. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.72) also stands out as a high-floor anchor; despite a standard platoon adjustment, he faces a soft matchup against Rea, making him a prime candidate for power production. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Jacob Wilson** (66.23) continue to provide excellent value, with park factors and situational placement at the top and middle of the order, respectively, driving their output deep into the \"Strong\" range.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Nolan Schanuel** (57.80), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Wade Meckler** (45.04). While **Nolan Schanuel** boasted a superior total score and a strong park factor against J.T. Ginn, the optimizer prioritized the positional versatility and lineup composition flexibility offered by the rest of the starting nine. Elsewhere, risks remain prominent; **Gunnar Henderson** (64.29) faces an elite challenge in Yoshinobu Yamamoto, though the combination of a favorable wind and an advantageous spot in the order keeps his efficiency high. Similarly, while **Jackson Merrill** (47.57) and **Drake Baldwin** (50.38) occupy the lower end of our starting confidence, they are preserved in the lineup to hedge against game cap attrition, provided they navigate the tricky left-handed matchups against Gore and Harrison without significant setbacks.",
